 - 2026-06-16: PHASE B1 (UNBLOCK the §5 in-generation thesis; harness-first BUILD) -- build + GATE a learned PARTIAL-STATE diffusion scorer for DiffusionGemma masked canvases, with a LEAK audit. .396 (exp4281) BLOCKED the in-generation moat with honest_verdict cannot_score_partial_states: no learned Carnot verifier can score PARTIAL (masked) DiffusionGemma denoising states. Standard PRMs are 'brittle or ill-calibrated' on masked states because they assume a left-to-right prefix (Prism, arXiv:2602.01842). BUILD the missing capability: a small learned value head over masked canvases (Manta-LM 2605.14531 closed-loop control template) that exposes score_partial_state(canvas, step) -> energy, trained on final exact-grid outcomes via the llama.cpp PR binary (~/.cache/llama.cpp-master/build/bin/llama-diffusion-gemma-eval). CRITICAL harness-first deliverable: a PASSING test that the scorer scores partial states NON-DEGENERATELY on a HELD-OUT fixture (partial_state_auroc > 0.6 on held-out canvases) -- NOT the full guidance run (that is exp4293, gated on this). CRITICAL leak audit: if partial-target labels LEAK the final answer (the scorer just reads the canvas's revealed cells = the answer), the rerun is CIRCULAR not a learned external moat -- emit partial_state_leak_free BARE bool from a leak ablation (mask the answer-bearing cells; if the scorer still scores, it is leak-free). verifier_is_oracle=false. NO TRM training; an honest partial_state_scorer_built=false (cannot build a non-degenerate, leak-free scorer) is COMPLETE and gates exp4293 off. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: partial_state_diffusion_scorer_built_leak_free; results/experiment_4292_partial_state_diffusion_scorer_build.json
 - 2026-06-16: PHASE B2 (the §5 in-generation headline; GATED on exp4292 leak-free build) -- DiffusionGemma energy-guided full run USING the learned partial-state scorer + matched no-Carnot-verifier controls. GATED on exp4292 partial_state_scorer_built==true AND partial_state_leak_free==true (no point running a guided benchmark without a leak-free scorer). Wire the exp4292 partial-state scorer as a per-step GUIDANCE energy reweighting DiffusionGemma's denoising token selection via the llama.cpp PR binary. On a REASONING corpus (FoVer-step/math, where the verifier is NOT the executable oracle), n>=30 per arm, run four conditions: unguided / RFG (arXiv:2509.25604, the model's OWN log-likelihood-ratio self-guidance -- the NO-external-verifier control) / EntRGi (arXiv:2602.05000) / Carnot-partial-state-guided. Add a guidance-dynamics diagnostic (arXiv:2506.10971: mask entropy, token-change covariance, trajectory stability) that rejects an over-guided scorer. Emit diffusiongemma_guidance_moat BARE bool := (Carnot-guided - RFG > 0 AND CI95-excl-0). verifier_is_oracle=false. The deepest open §5 question: does an EXTERNAL learned verifier IMPROVE generation, beating the model's own self-guidance? NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: diffusiongemma_guidance_moat_won; results/experiment_4293_diffusiongemma_energy_guided_run_partial_state.json
 - 2026-06-16: PHASE D1 (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING -- the mandated self-learning experiment; fix the .396 bug) -- re-run online verifier-weight adaptation with the Tier-2 arm FIXED + a retrieval-augmented arm. research-program.md mandates >=1 self-learning experiment/milestone (Tier-1 = online counter updates, CPU, <1us/update). .396 (exp4283) reported powered static-is-the-ceiling BUT was FLAGGED TAUTOLOGY because the Tier-2 arm was a NO-OP (tier2_cross_family_delta == static_cross_family_delta == 0.5 exactly) -- so the powered null is SUSPECT (the tier-2 mechanism did nothing). FIX the Tier-2 constraint-memory arm so it is a genuinely distinct mechanism (cache per-generator selection patterns, reuse on the nearest-neighbor seen generator), AND add a Tier-2 RETRIEVAL-augmented selector-context arm (Decocted 2604.04373: retrieval-only context on held-out families, NO weight mutation, NO LoRA). Re-run across the combined family set (the .395 manifest + exp4291's non-degenerate ARC-GEN generators, a soft input). Report static vs online vs tier2-memory vs tier2-retrieval cross-family delta + a POWERED CI95 on (best-adaptive - static). Emit online_adaptation_helps BARE bool := (best-adaptive - static > 0 AND CI95-excl-0). verifier_is_oracle=false. NO fine-tuning; NO TRM; NO live-LoRA. A null WITH a working tier-2 = static is genuinely the ceiling (retire the ask). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: adaptive_self_learning_improves_generalization; results/experiment_4295_self_learning_tier2_fixed_retrieval.json
